   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Status of Implementation Progress: At least 80% of managers (N = 80), including 100% of all female managers, are targeted for training in Certificate IV leadership and management. Current discussions are ongoing within DHERST on the training plan and arrangements. The plan IS incorporated in the 2025 annual work and financial planning.

DHERST conducted induction workshop for all 10 TVET colleges on the governance and management manual in each of the governing councils of the project TVET colleges. Future induction of new officers which may be appointed to replace those who may retire will be supported under the project.

The GESI action plan will be developed to include support for project TVET colleges in attracting and recruiting female managers and teachers and will be completed in 2025. Preparing for gender and disability inclusion sensitization among colleges; roll-out of meetings to gather feedback on DHERST GESI toolkit is scheduled in Q4 2025.

The 10 project TVET colleges regularly prepare their annual plans which need to be improved for more gender-responsiveness and to be more aligned with their respective strategic plans.

The 10 project TVET colleges will have to comply with annual audited financial and performance reporting requirements in line with the Governance Manual. Project checklist to assess the level of preparedness of the colleges rolled out to the colleges.

Following the engagement of the Technical Support team:

(i) At least 160 teachers (at least 75% of all female teachers) of construction trades and agriculture in project TVET colleges are targeted to receive technical upskilling; pedagogical upskilling, ICT skills training, and training on soft and life skills, and have an understanding of work-based learning and assessment; and specialized training on climate change.

(ii) At least 100 teachers (at least 75% of all female teachers) of construction trades and agriculture in project TVET colleges will participate in the pilot industry exchange program.

(iii) New content of teacher training in construction trades and agriculture in project TVET colleges includes gender-responsive and socially inclusive approaches, green technologies for climate change adaptation, and digitalization will be developed.

(iv) At least 20 demand-driven training courses (and at least 2 per TVET college), including new teaching and learning materials that mainstream gender-responsive and socially inclusive approaches, ICT and digitalization, and climate change, will be developed for newly introduced courses in construction trades and agriculture in project TVET colleges.

(v) At least 50 existing courses in construction trades and agriculture will be revised to be demand-driven and mainstreaming gender-responsive and socially inclusive approaches, ICT and digitalization, and climate change in project TVET colleges.

(vi) At least 4 gender-responsive bridging courses will be developed in construction trades and agriculture in project TVET colleges.

(vii) At least 50 teachers (at least 75 of all female teachers) will be trained in the development of gender-responsive and socially inclusive and climate change-resilient curricula in construction trades and agriculture in project TVET colleges.

The first of the three national forums was conducted on November 5-6, 2024 and yearly thereafter until 2026.At least 10 cooperation agreements are targeted to be signed between project TVET colleges and agriculture or construction enterprises or groups.

Ongoing mapping of available industries and skills needs to identify what opportunities for a potential cooperation agreement could be explored by each of the colleges.

The national TVET gender and social inclusion implementation plan will be developed and validated with the use of the Gender and Social Inclusion Toolkit by DHERST anticipated in Q4 2025.

GESI Capacity building series will be conducted in March-October 2025. Monitoring and follow through will be conducted quarterly from April to December 2025.

At least five gender-responsive and climate resilient women&apos;s dormitories will be upgraded/constructed in project TVET colleges as soon as the DNS team is in place and will follow the schedule in 4a. All project TVET colleges will prepare their operation and maintenance plans with detailed budget annually. Project checklist to assess the level of preparedness of the colleges have been rolled out to the colleges.

At least 160 gender-responsive and socially inclusive and climate resilient infrastructure assets will be upgraded or built for construction trades and agriculture programs in project TVET colleges.

Design services will start as soon as the Design and Supervision Firm (DNS) is contracted Q2 2025. The DNS will prepare the detailed engineering designs for the proposed infrastructure and cost estimates, including procurement assistance from Q1-Q4 2025. The remaining two years will be for construction and supervision and assistance during defects liability period up to Q1 2027. The civil works procurement for the 10 Colleges are expected to start Q3 to Q4 2025. Some of the civil works construction will be expected to commence in Q1 to Q2 2026.

The equipment provision plan is being developed and will be completed in Q2 2025 for implementation in each of the project TVET colleges, which supports their new construction trades and agriculture training programs. This will include Package 1-IT equipment to be procured in 4 batches. Issuance and submission from November 19, 2024, for supplier to be contracted in March 2025. Package 2 will be workshop equipment for replacement; list to be finalized with the colleges with technical specifications from Q1-Q2 2025. Procurement and contracting will be Q3-Q4 2025. Package 3 will be new equipment based on the new and revised curriculum; list and technical specifications will be finalized in Q4 2025 and will be procured in Q1-Q2 2026.Bids for the 4 batches of IT equipment have been received. Two contracts have been signed while the other 2 are nearing contract award.</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
